-- title:
--   Powers of the weighted centre contract from the blow-up chart
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q \ge 5$, a nonzero natural number $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$, and a prime $\ell \ge 3$ with $\ell \ne q$ and $\ell \nmid M'$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic $0$ and $\xi \in L$ a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity; the hypothesis `hι` asserts the existence of a ring homomorphism $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota(\xi) = e^{2\pi i/(q\ell)}$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L \subseteq L((T))$ (Laurent series over $L$), and `hK` requires that $K =$ [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.xHFunctionField ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH (q*ℓ) M'))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), that is, $K$ is generated over $L$ by the coefficientwise image under $\mathbb{Q} \to L$ of the $q$-expansion function field of the modular curve of level $N_0 = (q\ell)^2M'$ attached to the subgroup $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/N_0)^\times$ which is the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/(q\ell)^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q\ell)^\times$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q\ell$.
--
--   Let $A$ be a henselian discrete valuation ring which is a domain with fraction field $L$ and with algebraically closed residue field, such that $q \in \mathfrak m_A$ (`hAq`) and $\xi$ lies in the image of $A$ (`hξA`), and let $K$ be an $A$-algebra compatibly with $A \to L \to K$. Let $j \in K$, $j \ne 0$, whose Laurent series is the coefficientwise image in $L$ of the $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) of the modular $j$-function (`hj`). Let $\varpi \in A$ generate $\mathfrak m_A$ (`hϖ`), and let $\varpi_t \in A$ satisfy $\varpi_t^{q^2-1} = qu$ for some unit $u$ of $A$ (`hϖt`).
--
--   Write $C :=$ `chartAlgFin A ↥K j`, the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ of elements integral over $A[j]$, and `jChartFin A ↥K j` for $j$ viewed in $C$. Let $y \subseteq C$ be a maximal ideal (`hy`) containing the image of $\varpi$ (`hϖy`) and supersingular in the sense of `hss`: for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi : C \to \Omega$ with kernel $y$, the element $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), the set of those $j_0 \in \Omega$ for which every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\Omega$ with $j$-invariant $j_0$ has no nonzero affine point killed by $q$. Let $X :=$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A ↥K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) be the scheme obtained by glueing $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the $j$-chart algebra $C$ and $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the $j^{-1}$-chart algebra along the middle chart, with structure morphism `toBase` to $\operatorname{Spec} A$.
--
--   Throughout, for $\gamma \in SL(2,\mathbb{Z})$, a *level automorphism attached to $\gamma^{-1}$* means an $L$-algebra automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ satisfying [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.IsLevelAutAt L (q*ℓ) ξ (q*ℓ) ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH (q*ℓ) M') γ⁻¹ K τ`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L29): for every weight $k$, every pair $f,g$ of modular forms of weight $k$ on the group $\Gamma_H(N_0)$ viewed in $GL_2(\mathbb{R})$, every pair of power series $p_f,p_g$ over $\mathbb{Z}$ which are integral $q$-expansions of $f$ and $g$ with the Laurent series of $p_g$ nonzero, every $x \in K$ whose Laurent series is the image under [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) of $p_f/p_g$, and every ring homomorphism $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ sending $\xi$ to $e^{2\pi i/(q\ell)}$, the coefficientwise $\iota$-image of the Laurent series of $\tau x$, multiplied by the $q$-expansion of $g\mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}(q\ell)(\gamma^{-1})$, equals the $q$-expansion of $f\mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}(q\ell)(\gamma^{-1})$, where $\mathrm{conjElemN}\,m\,\delta = \begin{pmatrix} a & b/m \\ mc & d\end{pmatrix}$ for $\delta = \begin{pmatrix} a & b \\ c& d\end{pmatrix}$.
--
--   The hypothesis `hArig` (a rigidity hypothesis, its conclusion consisting of seven clauses, summarised here) asserts: for every point $z$ of $X$, every germ $\varpi_z$ at $z$ of the image of $\varpi$ under `toBase` lying in the maximal ideal of the stalk $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$, and every point $y'$ of $\operatorname{Spec} C$ mapping to $z$ whose ideal satisfies the same supersingularity condition as in `hss`, there exist a complete discrete valuation domain $W$, a ring homomorphism $\sigma : A \to W$ with $\mathfrak m_W = (\sigma\varpi)$, power series $f,u,v \in W[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u,v$ units and $f - (X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1) \in (X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$ (the Drinfeld form [`DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart.drinfeldForm q W`](def/DrinfeldCurve_LocalChart.html#L18)), and a ring isomorphism $e$ from the adic completion of $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$ onto $S := W[[X_0,X_1]]/(C(\sigma(\varpi_t^{q+1}))v - fu)$, such that, writing `toC` for the completion map, `mkS` for the quotient map onto $S$ and `germY` for the canonical map $C \to \mathcal{O}_{X,z}$: (1) $e$ carries the germ of each $a \in A$ to the class of $C(\sigma a)$; (2) every level automorphism $\tau$ attached to $\gamma^{-1}$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ maps $C$ into $C$; (3) if moreover $\gamma \in \Gamma(\ell)$, then $\tau a - a \in y'$ for all $a \in C$; (4) for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and such a $\tau$ preserving $C$ and acting trivially on $C/y'$, there are a ring automorphism $\theta$ of $S$, an element $c \in W$ and a matrix $M \in M_2(W)$ with $\theta \circ (e \circ \mathrm{toC} \circ \mathrm{germY}) = (e \circ \mathrm{toC} \circ \mathrm{germY}) \circ \tau|_C$, with $\theta$ fixing all constants $C(w)$, with $\theta(X_{j}) \equiv \sum_i C(M_{ij})X_i$ modulo the square of the ideal generated by the classes of $X_0,X_1$, with $c^{q+1} \equiv 1$ and $M_{ij} \equiv c\,\gamma_{ij}$ modulo $\mathfrak m_W$, with $c \equiv 1 \bmod \mathfrak m_W$ when $\gamma \in \Gamma(\ell)$, and with $c \not\equiv 1 \bmod \mathfrak m_W$ when $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau \ne \mathrm{id}$; (5) two prime ideals $P_1,P_2$ of $S$, each omitting at least one of the classes of $X_0,X_1$, each containing the class of $C(\sigma\varpi)$, and each containing an element of the form $a_iX_0 + b_iX_1 + h_i$ with $h_i \in (X_0,X_1)^2$ and $a_i,b_i \in \mathbb{Z}$, have distinct contractions to $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$ along $e \circ \mathrm{toC}$ whenever $q \nmid a_1b_2 - a_2b_1$; (6) for a prime $P$ of $S$ as in (5) containing an element $X_0 + h$ with $h \in (X_0,X_1)^2$, an element $a \in C$ has $\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germY}(a))$ in the contraction of $P$ along $e$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient of $a$ is the image of an element of $\mathfrak m_A$; (7) the series [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L (q*ℓ)`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) (the image of `jqModC L` under `qExpand L (q*ℓ)`) lies in $K$ and in $C$, and there are $a_0 \in A$ with the difference of its class and that of $a_0$ in $y'$, an integer $e_0 \ge 1$ and $h \in (X_0,X_1)^{e_0}$ such that $\sum_{i=0}^{e_0}\mathrm{coeff}_{(i,\,e_0-i)}(h)\,a^i b^{e_0-i}$ is a unit of $W$ for all $a,b \in W$ not both in $\mathfrak m_W$ with $a^qb - ab^q \in \mathfrak m_W$, and such that $e$ of $\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germY}(\cdot))$ of that difference is the class of $h$.
--
--   Next a particular such configuration is fixed: a point $z$ of $X$ with germ $\varpi_z$ of $\varpi$ (`hϖz`) in the maximal ideal of $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$ (`hz`), a point $y'$ of $\operatorname{Spec} C$ over $z$ (`hy'`) satisfying the supersingularity condition `hss'` and with $y'$ equal to $y$ as an ideal (`hy'y`), together with a witness for it: a complete discrete valuation domain $W_1$, a homomorphism $\sigma_1 : A \to W_1$ with $\mathfrak m_{W_1} = (\sigma_1\varpi)$ (`hσ₁`), power series $f_1,u_1,v_1 \in W_1[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u_1,v_1$ units (`hu₁`, `hv₁`) and $f_1$ congruent to the Drinfeld form modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$ (`hf₁`), and an isomorphism $e_1$ of the adic completion of $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$ with $S := W_1[[X_0,X_1]]/(C(\sigma_1(\varpi_t^{q+1}))v_1 - f_1u_1)$. The hypothesis `hW₁` asserts, for this witness, exactly the seven clauses (1)–(7) listed above.
--
--   The weighted centre $J$ is an ideal of $C$ pinned by `hJ`: $J$ is the infimum of the set of those ideals $J'$ of $C$ for which there exist $\gamma \in SL(2,\mathbb{Z})$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, and a level automorphism $\tau$ attached to $\gamma^{-1}$ mapping $C$ into $C$, with $J'$ the preimage under the restriction of $\tau$ to $C$ of the contraction along $e_1 \circ \mathrm{toC} \circ \mathrm{germY}$ of the ideal of $S$ generated by the classes of $C(\sigma_1\varpi_t)$, $X_0$ and $X_1$.
--
--   Finally, $B$ is the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ specified by `hB` as the $C$-subalgebra generated by $\{x \in K : \exists i \in J,\ x\,\varpi_t = i \text{ in } K\}$, i.e. $B = C[J/\varpi_t]$; and $W$ is a valuation subring of $K$ containing $B$ (`hBW`). Four further groups of hypotheses are imposed. `hR1`: $C \le B$, and every $f \in K$ can be written $f = g/h$ with $g,h \in B$, $h \ne 0$. `hR2`: $B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A$, and $B/\varpi B$ has Krull dimension at most $1$. `hR3` (five clauses): an element of $L$ lies in $W$ if and only if it comes from $A$; $\mathfrak m_W$ is generated by the image of $\varpi$; $W$ is a discrete valuation ring; an element of $C$ lies in $y$ if and only if it lies in $W$ and in $\mathfrak m_W$; and $f \in K$ lies in $W$ if and only if $f = g/h$ with $g,h \in B$ and $h \notin \mathfrak m_W$. `hEQ` (five clauses, summarised here): for every $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$-algebra structure on the residue field $k$ of $A$ there is a surjective ring homomorphism $\rho$ from $B$ onto [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q k`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) (the quotient of $k[X_0,X_1]$ by the ideal generated by `drinfeldPoly q k - 1`) whose kernel is the set of $b \in B$ lying in $\mathfrak m_W$, which is compatible with the residue map on $A$, and which is equivariant for level automorphisms: for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau$ attached to $\gamma^{-1}$ with $W$ stable under $\tau$, there are $c \in \mathbb{F}_{q^2}^\times$ with $(\mathrm{redQ}_q\gamma, c)$ in [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276) (the kernel of the character $(\bar\gamma,c) \mapsto \det(\bar\gamma)c^{q+1}$) such that $\rho \circ \tau$ is `hAction` of this element composed with $\rho$, and $c \ne 1$ whenever $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau \ne \mathrm{id}$; every level automorphism attached to some $\gamma^{-1}$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ maps $B$ into $B$; every prime $Q$ of $B$ containing $\varpi$ is reached by some level automorphism attached to $\gamma^{-1}$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$, in the sense that every $b \in B$ lying in $\mathfrak m_W$ has $\tau b \in B$ and $\tau b \in Q$; an element $b \in B$ whose images under all such $\tau$ lie in $\mathfrak m_W$ is divisible by $\varpi$ in $B$; and, for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau$ attached to $\gamma^{-1}$, if $\tau$ preserves $y$ then $W$ is stable under $\tau$.
--
--   Under these hypotheses the conclusion is: for every natural number $n$ and every $c \in C$, if there exists $b \in K$ with $b \in B$ and $c = \varpi_t^{\,n} b$ in $K$ (with $\varpi_t$ taken via $A \to K$), then $c \in J^{\,n}$. Equivalently, $C \cap \varpi_t^{\,n}B \subseteq J^{\,n}$, the reverse inclusion being immediate from the definition of $B$.
--
--   This is the contraction (saturation) step for the blow-up chart $B = C[J/\varpi_t]$ of the weighted centre $J$ at a supersingular point of the $j$-chart: it says that an element of the chart algebra divisible by $\varpi_t^{\,n}$ in $B$ already lies in $J^{\,n}$, so that $J^{\,n} = C \cap \varpi_t^{\,n}B$ and $\varpi_t$ is a regular parameter for the Rees algebra of $J$. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.exists_pow_mem_centre_pow_of_labelUnit_of_end_blowupChart`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.exists_pow_mem_centre_pow_of_labelUnit_of_end_blowupChart) in the analysis of the supersingular fibre of the auxiliary-level modular curve via the Drinfeld curve.
